![siam1](/wp-content/uploads/2012/02/siam1.jpg)![20080912053830-lydia-lunch-queen-of-siam-](/wp-content/uploads/2012/02/20080912053830-lydia-lunch-queen-of-siam.jpg)

Definitely Lydia Lunch’s best and most listenable work “Queen of Siam”, also her debut solo record, kicks straight in the balls. Queer lolita vocals, jazz, cabaret, avant-garde, depraved lyrics, dirty 80s guitars and sax, tension and tease… you got it all.

How would I describe it with one word? BADASS.

Here is my personal TOP 3 from this cult jewel. However, I recommend to enjoy it best in its full entirety:

3: “Lady Scarface”

\[youtube http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UkGcTW4w4\_o&w=560&h=315\]

2: “Spooky”

\[youtube http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SzQIvXQdJVQ&w=560&h=315\]

1: “Knives in the drain”

\[youtube http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tYeyVHOz950&w=420&h=315\]

